# The CA bundles that source-mysql, source-mysql-batch, source-postgres and
# source-postgres-batch trust when they verify a server. Listing the capture
# team here also has it requested for review on the automated refresh PRs from
# .github/workflows/cloud-cas.yaml, which the workflow's own token cannot
# request from a team.
/go/cloudcas/ @estuary/capture

# Changes to these files can let a connector image with a HIGH or CRITICAL
# vulnerability ship, either by adding an exception or by weakening or
# disabling the image scan, so they need operations' approval. The first
# pattern covers the root exceptions, which apply to every image, and each
# connector's own. This file is listed too, so the ownership itself cannot be
# removed without that approval.
**/.trivyignore.yaml                      @estuary/operations
/trivy.yaml                               @estuary/operations
/.github/workflows/image-scan.yaml        @estuary/operations
/.github/actions/scan-images/             @estuary/operations
/.github/scripts/trivy-scan.sh            @estuary/operations
/.github/scripts/test_trivy_scan.py       @estuary/operations
/.github/scripts/published-images.sh      @estuary/operations
/.github/CODEOWNERS                       @estuary/operations
